{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses","id":548706,"title":"Covenant Bonuses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-10T08:48:53-07:00","id":548706,"title":"Covenant Bonuses","content":"Hi everyone =D<br /> <br /> I&quot;m sure this is scrubbish and I apologize if my ineptness aggravates anyone. Little bit of backstory on me to help ease the pain. I've never GM'd although I'm working on a game. I only really played in one chronicle in a small group. Originally started with VtM then converted to VtR. I was horribly upset about the change to Malkavians and the lack of Dementation, especially Passions. However, the GM let my character stay the same and I was able to get Passions as a devotion (mixture of Majesty and Nightmares). We also never really got into the political aspects of the covenants. They were just there for bonuses. (also note, have yet to do anything with 2E (B&amp;S), but hoping to soon)<br /> <br /> So, my question is. What is suppose to be enticing about Invictus/Carthians/Unaligned/Belial's Brood. Other than having a group of people to hang out with, potentially providing benefits that social merits can cover. What would draw a player to these covenants other than they follow their character's belief's/political views? <br /> <br /> Especially with Ordo Dracul. Being able to prevent frenzy, always abel to feed from animals, use less blood upon waking. Those are HUGE draws to players that want their character to live/have more control.<br /> <br /> So as stated, what entices PLAYERS (not characters) to join factions like the Invictus/Carthians/etc.<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:25:07-07:00","id":548801,"title":"","content":"The game is generally meant to be played with those political elements. It's like asking why someone would take status (police) if there's no police force.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:09:59-07:00","id":548906,"title":"","content":"Thanks Michael.<br /> <br /> So, basically the draw is to players who like the political side of the game. So long as there really is one and it's not hack and slash based. However with your example, the merit for police, I've never had a game where police weren't involved so that could save your butt a lot in my opinion. Plus could give you the possibility of asking them for help and what-not.<br /> <br /> Still having a hard time seeing the draw other than &quot;It's what my character would do&quot;. Then kind of wishing I had Coils of Blood so I don't need to rely on being near civilization to eat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:12:05-07:00","id":548927,"title":"","content":"Also, just in case I wasn't clear (just noticed a thread about Invictus merits), I have only played/read from core books. Haven't even played from 2E yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:16:59-07:00","id":548936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses?p=548801#post548801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game is generally meant to be played with those political elements. It's like asking why someone would take status (police) if there's no police force.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's his point. The benefits derived from belonging to those groups are obtained by merits everyone can buy, regardless of affiliation.<br /> <br /> And to answer the original question, with the exception of the Carthians getting Carthian Law merits and the ability to covenant hop with impunity, there really is no unique benefit to having covenant status outside the Eldritch Trifecta. <br /> In VtR, it used to be the Unaligned were not subject to the effects of status (You couldn't use city or covenant status in rolls against them.) but currently there's nothing. And transporting that would make them virtually immune to Carthian Law effects which entails stripping status from others or using their status (or their victim's) as a metaphysical weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:18:57-07:00","id":548943,"title":"","content":"Thanks Tsusasi<br /> <br /> Carthian Law Merits? Is that in 1E or 2E? Or in it's own book. Maybe I missed it or it's not there at all. Same with Eldritch Trifecta. Where can I find these?<br /> <br /> Thanks again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:31:26-07:00","id":548998,"title":"","content":"Carthian Law and the merits for that were originally in the Carthian covenant book. The concept was transported to 2nd edition, and made default material instead of optional. And many of the Carthian exclusive merits and devotions there were incorporated into 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> The Eldritch Trifecta is a term referencing the Circle of the Crone, Lancea Sanctum, and Ordo Dracul, as they are the three covenants that get different sorceries as covenant exclusive benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:58:54-07:00","id":549025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses#post548706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone =D<br /> <br /> I&quot;m sure this is scrubbish and I apologize if my ineptness aggravates anyone. Little bit of backstory on me to help ease the pain. I've never GM'd although I'm working on a game. I only really played in one chronicle in a small group. Originally started with VtM then converted to VtR. I was horribly upset about the change to Malkavians and the lack of Dementation, especially Passions. However, the GM let my character stay the same and I was able to get Passions as a devotion (mixture of Majesty and Nightmares). We also never really got into the political aspects of the covenants. They were just there for bonuses. (also note, have yet to do anything with 2E (B&amp;S), but hoping to soon)<br /> <br /> So, my question is. What is suppose to be enticing about Invictus/Carthians/Unaligned/Belial's Brood. Other than having a group of people to hang out with, potentially providing benefits that social merits can cover. What would draw a player to these covenants other than they follow their character's belief's/political views?<br /> <br /> Especially with Ordo Dracul. Being able to prevent frenzy, always abel to feed from animals, use less blood upon waking. Those are HUGE draws to players that want their character to live/have more control.<br /> <br /> So as stated, what entices PLAYERS (not characters) to join factions like the Invictus/Carthians/etc.<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Well, like tsuasi said, the default assumption is that you're going to engage in politics. That's kind of a necessary buy-in with Vampire. You're a social predator, swimming in a bloody tank filled with cut-throat sharks. Vampire is primarily a social game, that's its draw. So, when you're making characters, mostly you're going to be thinking about what kind of character you want to play, what your goals are, etc. So, if your goal is to amass power, then you're drawn to the Invictus, etc. <br /> <br /> As for the draw? Every covenant comes with mystical bonuses. Even in 1st edition, this was true. There's huge benefits for no matter what way you go. Each covenant also represents a different kind of vampire. Want the classical pseudo-victorian aristocracy? Invictus. Want to play a new age vampire in touch with humanity and its evolution? Carthians. Golconda seeker? Ordo dracul. Children of Lilith or another monstrous being? Etc. <br /> <br /> Each of the five covenants are more than just their mystical benefits; it wouldn't be the first time someone played a covenant member without buying any sorcery or merits. The covenants are iconic vampire personalities. They're the kind of vampires you get from the wide variety of stories out there. And that's the real point - you play a member of the Invictus because you want to be the Undead Masters of the Night. You want to play Carthians because you want to be the rebels. You play the Brood because you want to be a hellrazer. And so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:04:46-07:00","id":549030,"title":"","content":"Players in my group tend to be drawn to the Covenants that will work with their character's goals. My players who loves magical stuff and pagan elements gravities towards the Circle of the Crone while my player who enjoys political interplay and business dealings leans towards the Invictus. Personally I really like the shadowy spy games of the Ordo Dracul as well as their focus on transcending the vampiric condition.<br /> <br /> Membership in a Covenant helps a player emphasis their character view of the world, if one plays to the stereotypes. It can also be a fun way to play against type, such as having a character who was forced into a particular group but favors another. That sort of thing works get for intrigue and espionage style games; playing on loyalties and personal convictions.<br /> <br /> For mechanical insentives to go with the Carthains or the Invictus: In 1E Carthians and the Invictus got nice discounts on certain merits and gained semi-mystical abilities in their respective Covenant books. In 2E both Covenants have a merit set that their members based on said semi-mystical abilities from the previous eddition. They also have a suite of non-mystical merits exclusive to their members (which other Covenants now have as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:48:32-07:00","id":549098,"title":"","content":"You mentioned that you can get what Invictus gives you with just Allies and other social merits. This isn't really true. Or, it may be true, but it's also not entirely accurate.<br /> <br /> Allies gives you the ability to ask a few favors.<br /> Contacts lets you ask for information.<br /> <br /> Status, which is typically how membership is mechanically represented, gives you both of those. It also gives you access to the Covenant's resources and facilities. This is where the non-mystical Covenants shine.<br /> <br /> What does the Crone have for resources and facilities? A temple? A run-down shack or hole in the ground to sleep in?<br /> <br /> Ordo gives you a place to conduct experiments, maybe, sure.<br /> <br /> Invictus? Penthouses. Corporate ties. Blood-bound government officials and ghouled police officers. If you want power over the Kine, you go Invictus, because they have spent centuries setting up the strings to puppet the old kine power structures.<br /> <br /> Carthians are the same, I presume, but for the middle and lower classes. They may not have the raw political and financial power, but they have the ear of the masses.<br /> <br /> The power to call down favors from Bill Gates or your local Senator or whatever is not really any less than the power to summon a weapon made of your own blood. It's just more subtle. And where Covenant membership differs from social merits is flexibility. You can buy hundreds of Allies to mimic what the Invictus has access to in their power pool, or you can just ask your Covenant to help you get what you need.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Eldritch Trifecta&quot; simply does not have the pool of social contacts and material resources that the social Covenants do.<br /> <br /> It may not be a concrete &quot;here is your magic spells&quot; benefit, though they do get unique Merits, but it's still a solid benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:49:51-07:00","id":549102,"title":"","content":"It's probably worth noting that being a member of Belial's Brood automatically makes a vampire cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:53:15-07:00","id":549114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses?p=549102#post549102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably worth noting that being a member of Belial's Brood automatically makes a vampire cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the vampire parrallel to smoking, really: makes you look cool and dramatic but tends to have side effects if used for extended periods of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T12:24:16-07:00","id":549147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses?p=549102#post549102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably worth noting that being a member of Belial's Brood automatically makes a vampire cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does it come with the leather jacket and motorcycle or do I have to provide my own?<br /> <br /> <br /> Maina, that's fantastic. I can understand that (not that I couldn't with any of the other responses, just that this one clicks something in my mind)<br /> <br /> That makes more sense. I will have to print that off for reference.<br /> <br /> So, I'm going to see about looking at the Carthian book, I'm curious about this covenant hoping. I do plan on reading it; however, from my experience the books aren't always the clearest. What is your opinion about it? Well, about covenant espionage in general. Can one say, join up with Ordo Dracul, learn some stuff, maybe a few coils or scales, then decide, &quot;Nah, Invictus man&quot;. Or simply a Carthian infiltrating either the Ordo or Invictus (I usually see those two as either in charge, or at least close to it).<br /> <br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:34:01-07:00","id":549240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses?p=549147#post549147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can one say, join up with Ordo Dracul, learn some stuff, maybe a few coils or scales, then decide, &quot;Nah, Invictus man&quot;. Or simply a Carthian infiltrating either the Ordo or Invictus (I usually see those two as either in charge, or at least close to it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Here there is a big difference between learning a few Coils and switching covenants, and infiltrating to learn Coils to teach them to your friends. In the latter case they <i>will</i> kill you. In the first case it would probably depend on your reasons for leaving and whether you are still on ok terms with your previous covenant. Maybe they will just put you under heavy Dominate to make you forget the most important secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:12:13-07:00","id":549340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses?p=549147#post549147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm going to see about looking at the Carthian book, I'm curious about this covenant hoping. I do plan on reading it; however, from my experience the books aren't always the clearest. What is your opinion about it? Well, about covenant espionage in general. Can one say, join up with Ordo Dracul, learn some stuff, maybe a few coils or scales, then decide, &quot;Nah, Invictus man&quot;. Or simply a Carthian infiltrating either the Ordo or Invictus (I usually see those two as either in charge, or at least close to it).</div> </div> </div> </div>You can; it's just difficult. The Covenants guard their secrets pretty tightly. Generally the anger you insight by stealing from a Covenant is greater than the gratitude that you gain for selling those secrets so traitors are most common at the lowest levels. Weirdly, this is also the most useless level to be a traitor. Say you show up at the local Circle of the Crone, having freshly betrayed the Lanca et Sanctum and you present your basic knowledge of dark miracles. Their response? Eh, seen it. Somebody probably already stole that a long time ago and they didn't really find it that useful because it's onle the most basic power.<br /> <br /> Usually to learn the bigger secrets (more than say one dot in blood sorcery or a single coil) you have to get invested in the Covenant. You get in what you put out, to borrow the Invictus saying. Once you are that deep into one of the Covenants it's unlikely that you really unlikely that you'd benefit too greatly from leaving it unless you ended up on an especially poor position. It's these usual situations, where something large might be betrayed, that can drive Covenant focused stories.<br /> <br /> For example, there's an example NPC in the Ordo book. Now, rank in the Ordo is largely measured by your Coils and by having Sworn an Oath to the Ordo Dracul, which is basically joinning a subfaction within the order. So, there's this guy. He's old, powerful, knows tons of Coils but he hasn't Sworn an Oath for the Covenant, which is a big deal for the Ordo. Thing is, no one will let him become Sworn now because it'll jump his rank up to basically the top of the Covenant since Sworn outrank similarly Coiled members. So his attempt to get an Oath are being blocked and he can't get much higher in Coils alone. So he's stuck and getting frustrated. It's this kind of situation where you might get a traitor if one of the other Covenants make him a better offer. Problem is, by the time you get to that point, what you actually want to only available within the Covenant you've already committed to. This guy might be able to go to the Invictus and sell out the secrets of the Order for a ton of money, status, herd, the finer things in life. But what he actually wants is the respect and fear of his academic peers and to study transcending the vampiric condition and the Invictus, for all it's money, can't every really give him that.<br /> <br /> As for the second, getting to an effective position within a Covenant takes alot of time, years for most individuals (PCs often being something of an exception). Sending somebody into the ranks of another Covenant to infiltrate it often ends one of two ways: the vampire never makes it very deep in and reports surface level intelligence or they get deep in through years of hard work and effort and eventually just decide to stay in their 'new' Covenant.<br /> <br /> The only group that seems to regularly make efforts in get inside of the great Covenants is Belial's Brood and they have a specific reason to hide who and what they are and have a goal of tearing down the entire system of Covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T17:49:56-07:00","id":549540,"title":"","content":"Players can find direction from covenants. They have people to give them adventure seeds and it is a safe environment for rivalry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T17:52:04-07:00","id":549543,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that in Second Edition, membership in multiple Covenants is fully permitted, with a few limitations. As long as your total dots in Covenant Status doesn't exceed 5, you can divide them however you want between multiple Covenants. Though, you can't have more dots in any other Covenant Status than you have in your primary. Basically, the Ordo Dracul doesn't mind you attending Sanctified Mass, and the Lancea et Sanctum doesn't mind having you there. But, the more involved you get with the Sanctum, the less the Ordo will be willing to trust you with prominent position. And, of course, if you teach any Coils to other Sanctified, or Theban Sorcery to other Dragons, they will kill you if they find out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:09:51-07:00","id":550365,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your replies! =D<br /> <br /> Okay so, as long as you play by their rules. Play nice, attained 'Mass' and any other social gatherings. Do work for them so long as it isn't directed at other covenants, you could in theory, be a part of all of them?<br /> <br /> Now, you say so long as you don't exceed 5 dots in status. May I ask why? Normally you can buy multiple Status merits, so why can't you have them separate? Ie:<br /> Status : Ordo Dracul 3<br /> Status : Circle of Crone 2<br /> Status: Invictus 2<br /> and so on and so on.<br /> <br /> Is there issues with that?<br /> <br /> Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:25:11-07:00","id":550374,"title":"","content":"City, Covenant, and Clan (why they specify Clan, as you can't have Status in other clans, is beyond me) are all capped the same way. You can have dots in more than one faction (City: San Francisco and City: San Diego, as an example), but the total for each type is capped at 5 (like, say, City: SF 3 and City: SD 2). You also cannot have more in an affiliate group than you have in your main one.<br /> <br /> The book does not explicitly spell out why, as far as I can find. I do think there is a good and likely reason: if you are dabbling in other organizations, your own is going to trust you less. Split loyalties do not make for leadership material. Likewise, the organizations that you're dabbling in will take supporters where they can, but without your primary loyalty, they are not going to share the majority of their resources with you.<br /> <br /> I suspect, though I cannot prove, that it's just an abstract representation of the social effects of splitting your loyalties. The Ordo may tolerate you taking part in Lancea services, but they'll never trust you quite like someone who dedicates themselves fully to their craft. Who knows what secrets you might spill after taking communion one too many times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:41:00-07:00","id":550560,"title":"","content":"That makes some sense to me.<br /> <br /> So in other terms, I can't have more than 5 of any status type merit. So if I play an undercover cop who infiltrates a gang, I can only have say, Status: Police 3, Status: Gang 2, and that's it? If so, I did not think it was so limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:13:10-07:00","id":550593,"title":"","content":"Nothing stops you from having <b><i>Allies: Covenant of Choice </i></b>to go along with your <i><b>Status: Covenant</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:36:38-07:00","id":550621,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Status implies membership.<br /> <br /> If you're going Undercover, then you probably lose access to your Status in your former Covenant, especially if you sever ties. If you have Status in both of them simultaneously, you didn't leave either of them, and have responsibilities to both.<br /> <br /> If you have a number of friends in a particular Covenant, then you should be using Allies to represent that, because you can ask them for a favor, you have no seniority over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:57:26-07:00","id":550660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses?p=550560#post550560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes some sense to me.<br /> <br /> So in other terms, I can't have more than 5 of any status type merit. So if I play an undercover cop who infiltrates a gang, I can only have say, Status: Police 3, Status: Gang 2, and that's it? If so, I did not think it was so limited.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It only applies to Clan, Covenant, and Kindred (City) Status.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'd think it'd be pretty hard, for instance, for the captain of a precinct to hold much of an undercover identity together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:24:21-07:00","id":550813,"title":"","content":"I think it has to do with the fact that Covenant Status is usually tied to specific positions of power within the Covenant. So, if you're a member of the Corus in the Circle of the Crone, the Lancea et Sanctum just ain't gonna let you be Archbishop. Too much potential for conflict of interest. The more involved you are with other Covenants, the less your Covenant is going to trust younwith leadership positions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-11-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:20:09-07:00","id":551022,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses?p=550660#post550660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That being said, I'd think it'd be pretty hard, for instance, for the captain of a precinct to hold much of an undercover identity together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol fair enough. Since status generally means position, ya I can see t hat being an issue.<br /> <br /> But question, can't you technically gain status without actually joining? If I hang out at an area long enough, get to know everyone. You start to develop clout in with that group no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T21:15:01-07:00","id":551062,"title":"","content":"You don't gain Status. That would be a great case for acquiring the new two dot merits from the <i>Secrets of the Covenants </i>playtest where you're a frequent collaborator, or for purchasing dots in Allies (Covenant). Actual Status should predicate on your joining them and holding a position of some kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T22:02:21-07:00","id":551106,"title":"","content":"Oh okay, thanks! <br /> <br /> One other thing, pertaining to the Allies merit actually. How specific does it go? Does 'Allies : Police' mean that I know Constable Riemert or maybe even Chief Francis? (I know that each dot represents a different ally, not necessarily their status in their respective group). Or does it simply mean that the offices that the local police station know my name and are friendly to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T22:03:08-07:00","id":551107,"title":"","content":"(I always had issues understanding some of the social merits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T23:00:22-07:00","id":551145,"title":"","content":"Allies is not Contacts, so the number of dots you have in a single instance of Allies is the level of cumulative favors you can ask of them without having to roll. Once the favor level exceeds your total dots in that instance of Allies, I believe the dice pool is Presence + Persuasion + Allies - Favor Level as a roll. On a success, you temporarily lose access to one dot of that instance of Allies, which returns at the end of the chapter (session).<br /> <br /> You can have multiple instances of Allies. Example: I have Allies 3 (Local Precinct) and Allies 2 (Los Zetas). I can ask for up to 3 1 dot favors of the Local Precinct without rolling. If I ask for a level 4 favor, or more than 3 level 1 favors, I have to roll. Each of these is a seperate instance of the merit, and costs 1 Experience per dot.<br /> <br /> What your Allies can do is narratively determined. For examples, Allies might be able to perform the Services listed on page 185-186 of the 2nd edition. These are examples of services that Allies could potentially acquire, but it shouldn't be the limit. Storytellers should hopefully feel comfortable improvising the level of cost of a service, based upon how hard it is for an organization to do, and how much they like the character using the merit.<br /> <br /> As a sidenote, Services might be acquired through other social merits as well. Status for instance could also do it, though it might be harder to convince them to render the service if its higher than that level of Status affords. Services are a neat little thing.<br /> <br /> The cost of some things might move up and down depending upon how easy it is for an organization to do it, or how you want it done. Doing something illegal might be a much higher favor from the Police, and might incur some complications, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:17:00-07:00","id":555709,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm apparently very rusty on the subject. I shall have to re-read! Thanks =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:09:59-07:00","id":555957,"title":"","content":"There can even be some overlap. Might be a good idea to keep a sheet with a note about each one that indicates what you can <i>do</i> with each one (favors, info, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:05:26-07:00","id":556046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/548706-covenant-bonuses?p=551107#post551107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I always had issues understanding some of the social merits)</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. It took me an embarrassingly long time to learn the differences between the various social merits that represent your relationships with people. Especially Allies vs. Contacts vs. Status. Here's a rundown for easy reference:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/483828-how-contacts-and-retainers-work?p=484179#post484179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To expand a little on the various types of &quot;people Merits&quot;, as I call them:<br /> <br /> <b>Allies:</b> a group of people you have pull with but are not yourself a member of. Each such group is rated 1 to 5, higher ratings means you can ask bigger favors of them.<br /> <b>Contacts:</b> a single person <i>or </i>a group of people you can tap for information. Each such person or group is a single dot. The more dots you have, the more different sources of information you can access.<br /> <b>Mentor:</b> a person who teaches or is willing to help your character. Each such person is rated 1 to 5, higher ratings means more knowledge or power they have or are willing to share with your character.<br /> <b>Retainer:</b> a single person who works for you (though not necessarily a literal employee) such as a personal assistant, butler, bodyguard, etc. Each such person is rated 1 to 5, higher ratings means more skilled labor.<br /> <b>Staff:</b> a group of people who work for you, such as wait staff, pit crew, etc. Each dot gives your Staff an additional task they can be called upon for.<br /> <b>Status:</b> a group of people you are a member of and hold sway within due to your rank. Each such group is rated 1 to 5, higher ratings means you have more power within that group.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:39:22-07:00","id":557136,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> I will definitely have to get a print-out of that/re-read them again. =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}